Chapter: BloomSceneKernel
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceMath

 The scene pass of the bloom demo: three bright coloured orbs orbiting on a dark
 field, one GPU thread per pixel. Each orb has a sharp bright core (its falloff
 cubed) so the highlights blow out to full white-hot colour -- exactly what the
 bloom pass will bleed into a glow. Output is a packed-RGB framebuffer that the
 second pass reads. Float falloff from DeviceMath.

 We say:

Section: Parameters

  bs-width : Integer = 1024
  bs-half-w : Integer = 512
  bs-half-h : Integer = 384

Section: Orb

 Contribution of one orb to a channel: a cubed radial falloff scaled by the
 orb's colour, in 0..255-ish (may exceed, the caller clamps).

  bs-fall : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Real
  bs-fall (px) (py) (cx) (cy) =
    let dx = real-from-int (px - cx)
    in let dy = real-from-int (py - cy)
    in let d2 = dx * dx + dy * dy
    in let inten = real-max 0.0 (1.0 - d2 / 4200.0)
    in inten * inten * inten

Section: Scene Kernel

  bloom-scene-step : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  bloom-scene-step (outb) (frame) (gid) =
    let px = gid - (gid / bs-width) * bs-width
    in let py = gid / bs-width
    in let f = real-from-int frame / 32.0
    in let x0 = bs-half-w + real-to-int (real-cos f * 300.0)
    in let y0 = bs-half-h + real-to-int (real-sin f * 175.0)
    in let x1 = bs-half-w + real-to-int (real-cos (f * 1.3 + 2.1) * 240.0)
    in let y1 = bs-half-h + real-to-int (real-sin (f * 1.3 + 2.1) * 250.0)
    in let x2 = bs-half-w + real-to-int (real-cos (f * 0.8 + 4.2) * 330.0)
    in let y2 = bs-half-h + real-to-int (real-sin (f * 0.8 + 4.2) * 150.0)
    in let a = bs-fall px py x0 y0
    in let b = bs-fall px py x1 y1
    in let c = bs-fall px py x2 y2
    in let r = a * 255.0 + b * 70.0 + c * 90.0
    in let g = a * 70.0 + b * 255.0 + c * 110.0
    in let bl = a * 60.0 + b * 120.0 + c * 255.0
    in let ri = real-to-int (real-min 255.0 (r + 6.0))
    in let gi = real-to-int (real-min 255.0 (g + 7.0))
    in let bi = real-to-int (real-min 255.0 (bl + 11.0))
    in act
    device-store outb gid (ri * 65536 + gi * 256 + bi)
    end
